\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou, Jesu, Thou my breast inspire,
\par And touch my lips with hallowed fire,
\par And loose a stammering infant's tongue;
\par Prepare the vessel of Thy grace,
\par Adorn me with the robes of praise,
\par And mercy shall be all my song:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Mercy for all who know not God,
\par Mercy for all in Jesu's blood,
\par Mercy, that earth and heaven transcend;
\par Love that o'erwhelms the saints in light,
\par The length, and breadth, and depth, and height
\par Of love divine which never ends !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A faithful witness of Thy grace,
\par Well may I fill the allotted space,
\par And answer all Thy great design;
\par Walk in the works by Thee prepared;
\par And find annexed the vast reward,
\par The crown of righteousness divine.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When I have lived to Thee alone,
\par Pronounce the welcome word: Well done !
\par And let me take my place above,
\par Enter into my Master's joy,
\par And all eternity employ
\par In praise, and ecstasy, and love.
\par \tab Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

